      "why": "The armored red block at R7C4 can never be hit where it is. The only hammer is the purple clockwise spinner at R3C3, and it needs two magnets. The blue magnet at R3C4 leaves upward and drags the first block behind it - once column 4 is clear, that is the red magnet at R6C4, which lands in R3C4, right beside the hammer, now pointing right with the hammer first behind it. When the red magnet then leaves, it turns the hammer and drags it into R3C4, facing down column 4 at the shell: ram, and the cracked block leaves to the left. The hammer must have been turned exactly three times by then (left - up - right - down): once by the blue magnet's escape, once by the yellow counter-clockwise spinner below it (R4C3) leaving, once by the red magnet's escape. Meanwhile it is free to leave several times, and the red magnet is free from the first move (it would drag the purple spinner at R6C2 instead). Checked over every winning line (2714): the blue magnet always fires before the red one; the hammer is turned and carried by a magnet that another magnet moved, then rams, on every line; only 2 of the 5 legal first moves keep the board solvable.",
